<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσχάρ-α</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσχαρ-άρη</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ἡ, 
			Ep.
		 gen. and dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσχαρόφιν</span>
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ἐσχ</span>- <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			7.169
		</span></i>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἐσχ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.59
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				19.389
			</span></i>):—<i>hearth, fire-place,</i>
			
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑστία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (esp. in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μὲν ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάρῃ ἧστο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.52
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧσται ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάρῃ ἐν πυρὸς
				αὐγῇ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				305
			</span></i> ; of suppliants, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕζετ᾽ ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάρῃ ἐν κονίῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.153
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>pan of coals, brazier,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				888
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				938
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.94
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				95
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρώων πυρὸς ἐσχάραι</span>
			<i>watch-fires</i> of the camp, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.418
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sacrificial hearth</i> (hollowed out in the ground and so dist.
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμός,</span> structural altar, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμοί</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; used esp. in heroworship, <i><span class="en">
				Neanth.
				7J.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.420
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1016
			</span></i> : but freq. used generally, <i>altar of burnt-offering,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἐσχάραν Φοίβου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					205
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάρᾳ πυρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					108
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμένας ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάραις</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				806
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πυθική</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1240
				</span></i>
			 ; at Eleusis, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				59.116
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				37
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρακλειδῶν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.1658
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span> ; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βώμιοι
			ἐσχάραι</span> structured <i>altars,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				274
			</span></i> ; sometimes movable, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.3.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Callix.
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				13
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>fire-stick</i> (bored with the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρύπανον,</span> q. v.), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				5.9.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ign.</u>
				64
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>platform, stand, basis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				92.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.Mech.
				32.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				10.11.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>grating,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				27.4
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> Medic.,
				<i>scab, eschar</i> on a wound caused by burning or otherwise, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ἐκπτώσιας τῶν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				184.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				863a12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.315
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VI.</b> in pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ χείλη τῶν γυναικείων
					αἰδοίων</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1286
			</span></i>.</div>
